===Etymology===
{{inh+|ru|orv|граница}} attested in Southern Rus' since 1375 and speculated to be an Old Polish loan, even though there's no scholarly consensus, ultimately from {{der|ru|sla-pro|*granica}}. The more common Muscovite term was {{noncog|zle-mru|рубежъ}}, but it was to some extent displaced, perhaps under Polish and Ruthenian influence. {{surf|ru|грань|-и́ца}}.

